OL,3,GNEWSATeen swimmer sets sights on
OL,4,ASpecial Olympics glory
OL,5,
OL,6,FA nineteen-year-old swimmer has said he
OL,7,Fwill win "3,000 gold medals" in the
OL,8,FSpecial Olympics Great Britain.
OL,10,FSam Craddock, from Dorchester in
OL,11,FDorset, has Down's syndrome and will be
OL,12,Fcompeting in the 50m freestyle, 50m
OL,13,Fbreast stoke and 100m individual
OL,14,Fmedley.
OL,16,FThe event in Birmingham, between
OL,17,FThursday 27 and Sunday 30 August, will
OL,18,Fsee more than 1,000 athletes with
OL,19,Fintellectual disabilities compete
OL,20,Facross several sports.
OL,23,APub: 21-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB S Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
